+  // Fury: a profile's browser quits when its last window closes.
+  //
+  // macOS Chrome stays running with no windows, held by `_keepAlive`, until
+  // the person presses Cmd+Q. For a browser started by the Fury agent that
+  // left a second icon in the Dock and a profile the agent still counted as
+  // open -- which, for a team profile, also meant its session was not sent to
+  // the server until something else closed it (reported 08.10.2026). Each
+  // Browser holds a keep-alive of its own, so once a window exists this one
+  // is only what keeps the process up without any; releasing it here gives
+  // the Windows lifecycle, and the ordinary shutdown path with it. Nothing a
+  // page can observe changes.
+  //
+  // Released when the first window exists, which is not always by now: a
+  // profile restoring its session (the agent passes --restore-last-session)
+  // has none here and gets it a moment later. Checking only here kept the
+  // keep-alive for every profile after its first launch (reported
+  // 13.10.2026). A launch that never opens a window keeps it, as Chrome does.
+  _furyFirstBrowserObserver = std::make_unique<FuryFirstBrowserObserver>();
+  if (!GlobalBrowserCollection::GetInstance()->IsEmpty()) {
+    [self furyQuitWithLastWindow];
+  }
